  "caveats": ["There is no comprehensive global registry of non-binding MOUs, joint statements and joint initiatives. Every source here misses some of them: an empty cell means no agreement was found in these sources, not that no cooperation exists.", "Partnership depth classes are provisional rules over the coded agreements; keyword mentions in a broad joint statement never make an agreement operational.", "GSP documents run from 1992 to 2023, most before 2021; later agreements come from DESTA, the curated table and the memo evidence, which are selective.", "EU member states cooperate mostly through EU law and EU programmes, which these sources do not record as bilateral agreements between members; EU-level agreements are attributed to each member state (via the EU).", "Agreement gaps are labelled rules over the exported components (need, capability, recommendation, UN-vote alignment, stage-by-stage coverage), not a score. Complementarity between economies in opposite UN-vote blocs is flagged, not counted."]
